      "webpage": {
        "text": "[Photo] Buk-gu, Gwangju Provides Relief Supplies to Wildfire-Affected Areas\n\nPublished 28 Mar.2025 16:53(KST)\n\nUpdated 03 Jul.2026 10:48(KST)\n\nopen/close\n\nShare Language Text Size Print\n\nOn the 28th, Buk-gu, Gwangju urgently provided relief supplies to areas severely affected by large-scale wildfires, including Sancheong and Hadong in Gyeongnam. Buk-gu sent relief items worth a total of 52 million KRW, including 5,000 bottles of water, 2,000 pieces of bread, 315 boxes of ramen, 42,000 masks, and 300 blankets, loaded onto trucks and delivered to the affected areas that afternoon. Buk-gu plans to expand support sequentially, starting with the regions most severely damaged by the wildfires. Provided by Buk-gu, Gwangju.\n\n\n한글 기사 보기\n\nThis content was produced with the assistance of AI translation services.\n\n© The Asia Business Daily. All rights reserved. Unauthorized AI training and use prohibited.\n\n\nToday’s Briefing\n\n\nto Top",
